+# DRAFT — Act 32 Prospective Statistics Trial Clarification
+
+Status: proposal for independent Parliamentary sponsorship, red-team review and recorded vote. NOT ENACTED; this document authorizes no dispatch.
+
+## Problem and scope
+
+Act 32 amendment D is implemented as requiring a verified historical outcome numerator AND its measured resource cost before ANY office can start. On the shared billy-dev host, historical per-office CPU use cannot be reconstructed, and no matched independently verified outcome/cost window exists. Statistics was intended to make such evidence possible. Act 32 K meanwhile explicitly states that lack of positive evidence should not block the authorized first trial. It is dishonest to fill missing historical values with zero or to label whole-host CPU as measured per-office CPU.
+
+This proposal amends Act 32 D/E/H/K and clause 9 ONLY for the FIRST, bounded, reversible Statistics trial. It does not waive existing constitutional or budget rules, extend spending powers, change Judiciary case selection, or activate any office.
+
+## Proposed operative provisions
+
+1. Pretrial design: before FIRST Statistics dispatch the Executive must preregister the primary genuine-outcome endpoint, population, missingness and source-dependence checks, negative controls, alternative business-as-usual comparator, resource observation window and falsifiers. Freeze available original pretrial evidence and real contemporaneous resource measurements with source hashes. Declare unavailable historical values unavailable, not zero. A retrospectively verified historical outcome numerator or isolated per-office CPU accounting is NOT a prerequisite to this first measurement trial only. No effectiveness claim can be made from this exception.
+
+2. Pretrial spend controls: Economy must demonstrate testable per-office and aggregate token, wall-time and machine-resource hard limits including concurrent work, missing/reset counters, backend ambiguity, crash/reboot, deadline, expiry and in-flight termination. OpenCode session token increments and elapsed wall-time must be actually measured. Where reliable per-office CPU cannot be observed, the entire host busy CPU increment may be charged pessimistically to the Statistics trial as a conservative upper bound for safety, NOT labelled actual office CPU or a statistically valid marginal-cost estimate. Unknown meter state blocks new invocation; confirmed overruns require stop/wind-down with evidence. No arbitrary numerical worker-count cap is introduced.
+
+3. Independent launch gate: Judiciary independently inspects exact verified source bytes, negative tests, the budget guard, error handling, pretrial methodological plan and the bounded Executive order. It publishes an evidence-linked proceed/hold/stop safety finding; self-certification cannot satisfy it. Only then may the Executive authorize ONE Statistics-only window of at most 14 days with exact enacted Act, office, start, expiry, caps and rollback/reboot plan. The dispatch guard must deny wrong office/Act, missing review, overrun, expiry and malformed state, including after restart.
+
+4. Value is assessed AFTER measurement, not asserted at launch. Before any declaration that Statistics improves outcomes, any renewal, or progression to Foresight, Judiciary and the independent evaluator must confirm the real eligible-event numerator, source-independence/negative-controls, missing data, corresponding actual cost or defensible bound, uncertainty and opportunity cost against the pre-registered alternative. Agent runs, commits, reports, correspondence, predictions registered, detector clears and publications are not benefits. A missing result is inconclusive, not positive. Successors remain disabled without substantive signed positive evidence. Existing day-30 review, 45-day overall expiry rules, affirmative reauthorization and strict serial progression stay in force.
+
+5. Other institutions unchanged. Foresight's Act 22 ledger and Act 32 I calibration threshold, Strategy counterfactuals, Spying source restrictions, Post/Gazette non-authority and confidential fallback all remain unchanged. There is no change until a valid Parliamentary Act AND exact independently reviewed code with tests are deployed.
+
+## Mandatory falsifiers
+
+- No law, Executive order, Judiciary signoff, source inventory, working token meter or hard cap => no Statistics dispatch.
+- Missing/reset token/CPU counters; forged sender, wrong Act, spend overrun, crash, reboot, expired order or active backend ambiguity => no new dispatch and preserved incident evidence.
+- Whole-host CPU must be explicitly tagged UPPER_BOUND and never ACTUAL_OFFICE_CPU.
+- Unobserved outcome must be marked UNAVAILABLE, not zero.
+- No Foresight, Strategy or Spying, no renewal or efficacy claim, until independent posttrial outcome and resource evaluation establishes the positive predecessor gate.
+
+## Source facts, not authority
+
+- records/knowledge/statistics-trial-preflight-20261120.json shows honest not_ready state.
+- records/JUDICIARY-FACTUAL-DETERMINATION-2026-11-21-act32-e2big-repair.md independently verifies one material repair, but no paired cost denominator.
+- records/knowledge/STATISTICS-RESOURCE-BASELINE-20261121.md and owner-only 20261122-founder-pretrial snapshots measure real tokens and whole-host CPU but not actual per-office CPU or value.
+- government/knowledge-budget.sh and knowledge-budget.conf have safety controls but all four office configurations remain disabled.
+
+Sponsor, independent red-team, assumptions/falsifiers, proper Act 22 registration, ballots, tally and law codification remain Parliamentary obligations. The Founder priority comment on Antonina issue SvMHxlO6F1R6u3cQcr3lKA-repeated does not itself enact this text.
